   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "THE SETTING",
   "originalText": "THE SETTING",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00103",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 120,
   "y": 2587.0,
   "width": 557.9599999999999,
   "height": 195.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e9ecef",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00103",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 722,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1340,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Ramesh runs a kirana shop in Kurla. Roughly 400 people pay him in a month.\nAround 40 of them do not pay on the day — they take the atta and the oil\nand say they will settle on Friday, or after the 10th, or when the wages\ncome.\n\nHe writes it in a notebook by the till. A name and a number. Sometimes\nonly a number, because there are four people waiting.\n\nSharma walks out with no copy of anything. There are about 1.3 crore shops\nlike Ramesh's in India, and nobody — not RBI, not the NSS, not any\nconsultancy we could find — publishes how much money is sitting in those\nnotebooks tonight.",
   "originalText": "Ramesh runs a kirana shop in Kurla. Roughly 400 people pay him in a month.\nAround 40 of them do not pay on the day — they take the atta and the oil\nand say they will settle on Friday, or after the 10th, or when the wages\ncome.\n\nHe writes it in a notebook by the till. A name and a number. Sometimes\nonly a number, because there are four people waiting.\n\nSharma walks out with no copy of anything. There are about 1.3 crore shops\nlike Ramesh's in India, and nobody — not RBI, not the NSS, not any\nconsultancy we could find — publishes how much money is sitting in those\nnotebooks tonight.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00104",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 720,
   "y": 2558.25,
   "width": 95.69999999999999,
   "height": 18.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#ffd43b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00104",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 729,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1353,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "THE PROBLEM",
   "originalText": "THE PROBLEM",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00105",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 720,
   "y": 2587.0,
   "width": 557.9599999999999,
   "height": 260.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e9ecef",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00105",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 736,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1366,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The notebook has one author and two people's money in it.\n\nRamesh cannot see who is about to pay and who is drifting away, so he\ntreats them identically. Sharma, who has paid on day 9 every month for two\nyears, gets asked on day 4 and hears an accusation. Patil, who has quietly\nreached day 40, gets asked nothing because he has stopped coming in and is\ntherefore out of sight.\n\nSharma cannot see his own total. He owes money at three shops and could\nnot tell you the sum within ₹500. And if the notebook says ₹500 where he\nremembers ₹300, he has no entry, no date and no evidence. He simply loses.\n\nWhen it goes wrong, the only enforcement anyone has is embarrassment —\nbeing asked in front of other customers. The software that exists makes\nthat worse, not better: one live Indian product sells shopkeepers \"instant\ncommunity alerts when a chronic non-payer enters your neighborhood\".",
   "originalText": "The notebook has one author and two people's money in it.\n\nRamesh cannot see who is about to pay and who is drifting away, so he\ntreats them identically. Sharma, who has paid on day 9 every month for two\nyears, gets asked on day 4 and hears an accusation. Patil, who has quietly\nreached day 40, gets asked nothing because he has stopped coming in and is\ntherefore out of sight.\n\nSharma cannot see his own total. He owes money at three shops and could\nnot tell you the sum within ₹500. And if the notebook says ₹500 where he\nremembers ₹300, he has no entry, no date and no evidence. He simply loses.\n\nWhen it goes wrong, the only enforcement anyone has is embarrassment —\nbeing asked in front of other customers. The software that exists makes\nthat worse, not better: one live Indian product sells shopkeepers \"instant\ncommunity alerts when a chronic non-payer enters your neighborhood\".",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00106",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": 2558.25,
   "width": 113.1,
   "height": 18.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#ffd43b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00106",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 743,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1379,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "WHAT WE BUILD",
   "originalText": "WHAT WE BUILD",
   "fontSize": 15,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00107",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1320,
   "y": 2587.0,
   "width": 557.9599999999999,
   "height": 325.0,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#e9ecef",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00107",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 750,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1392,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "BAHI is the same notebook with a second reader.\n\nSharma scans a QR by the till once and he is in — the shop, and his own\nrunning balance. Ramesh speaks the entry to the Soundbox, because his\nhands are full: \"Sharma ko do sau udhaar.\" He can tag the man \"Room 19, B\nwing\", since he does not know his surname.\n\nSharma's phone buzzes. He taps Confirm. If he does not, the entry stays in\nRamesh's book marked unconfirmed — Ramesh never loses his record, but a\nconfirmed entry is a fact and an unconfirmed one is only a claim.\n\nThen the part that is actually new. Every night the agent works out, per\nperson, from that person's own history, when a reminder should go and how\nit should read. Sharma is left alone until day 7. Patil, forty days out\nand never before past thirty, gets a message that asks rather than\ndemands, because something in his life has changed and chasing him is both\ncruel and ineffective.\n\nThe reminder carries a UPI button. One tap and the entry closes on both\nsides at once.",
   "originalText": "BAHI is the same notebook with a second reader.\n\nSharma scans a QR by the till once and he is in — the shop, and his own\nrunning balance. Ramesh speaks the entry to the Soundbox, because his\nhands are full: \"Sharma ko do sau udhaar.\" He can tag the man \"Room 19, B\nwing\", since he does not know his surname.\n\nSharma's phone buzzes. He taps Confirm. If he does not, the entry stays in\nRamesh's book marked unconfirmed — Ramesh never loses his record, but a\nconfirmed entry is a fact and an unconfirmed one is only a claim.\n\nThen the part that is actually new. Every night the agent works out, per\nperson, from that person's own history, when a reminder should go and how\nit should read. Sharma is left alone until day 7. Patil, forty days out\nand never before past thirty, gets a message that asks rather than\ndemands, because something in his life has changed and chasing him is both\ncruel and ineffective.\n\nThe reminder carries a UPI button. One tap and the entry closes on both\nsides at once.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 1,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "text-a00108",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 1920,
   "y": 2558.25,
   "width": 339.29999999999995,
   "height": 18.75,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#ffd43b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "index": "a00108",
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 757,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1405,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updatedAt": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
