   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Every ledger app in India is one-sided. Khatabook has 5 crore shopkeepers\nand no customer app. OkCredit advertises the absence: \"Customer ko app ki\nzaroorat nahi.\" Paytm's own Business Khata, shipped in 2020, is one-sided\nand now sits orphaned off its product nav.\n\nTwo-sidedness needs both halves already installed, and one company in\nIndia has that.\n\nThe second difference is that we read the law first. Recording someone's\ndebt and then reminding them about it walks into four separate Indian\nstatutes, and each one became a single hard rule: the button acknowledges\nand never promises; not one rupee is charged above the price; debts are\nallowed to expire instead of being kept alive forever by our own prompts;\nand the reminder is never monetised and never shames.\n\nThat last one is not squeamishness. Under BNS s.308, threatening to expose\nsomeone unless they pay is extortion, and it carries seven years. The\ncompetition is already selling it.",
   "originalText": "Every ledger app in India is one-sided. Khatabook has 5 crore shopkeepers\nand no customer app. OkCredit advertises the absence: \"Customer ko app ki\nzaroorat nahi.\" Paytm's own Business Khata, shipped in 2020, is one-sided\nand now sits orphaned off its product nav.\n\nTwo-sidedness needs both halves already installed, and one company in\nIndia has that.\n\nThe second difference is that we read the law first. Recording someone's\ndebt and then reminding them about it walks into four separate Indian\nstatutes, and each one became a single hard rule: the button acknowledges\nand never promises; not one rupee is charged above the price; debts are\nallowed to expire instead of being kept alive forever by our own prompts;\nand the reminder is never monetised and never shames.\n\nThat last one is not squeamishness. Under BNS s.308, threatening to expose\nsomeone unless they pay is extortion, and it carries seven years. The\ncompetition is already selling it.",
